First Batch of Individual Pension Product Funds Launches Sales, Minimum Holding Period as Short as 360 Days - China News Society
First batch of individual pension product funds are launched for sale
The institution's 7 products can be selected, with the shortest holding period being 360 days.
Individual pension investment products have finally been launched.
On February 10th, China Wealth Management Network released the first list of individual pension product listings. Seven individual pension products from China Galaxy Securities, Agricultural Bank of China Wealth Management, and China Post Savings Bank Wealth Management will officially start selling.
By now, the "shelf" of individual pension accounts has finally gathered the four types of products: individual pension savings, individual pension investment, individual pension insurance, and public offering funds for individual pensions.
According to the introduction, the first batch of individual pension fund products are all public offering net value-type open-ended products. Among them, 5 new products and 2 existing products are included. Except for one product which is a hybrid product, the remaining 6 products are all fixed income products.
Beijing Youth Daily reporters saw that among the five new products issued, four came from the Industrial and Commercial Bank of China's wealth management department, all of which are fixed income products. The shortest holding periods were 365 days, 540 days, 720 days, and 1080 days, with corresponding performance benchmarks (annualized) of 3.70% - 4.20%, 4.10% - 4.60%, 4.40% - 4.90%, and 5.25% - 5.75% respectively.
The remaining new product is "Youting Wealth Addition · Hongjin Shortest Holding 1095 Days No. 1", which is also a fixed income product. It started fundraising on February 10th and ended on February 19th. Its risk rating is Level 2.
Among the two ongoing products, one is the "Nongyin Tongxin · Lingdong" 360-Day Innovation Technology RMB Wealth Management Product by Nongyin Securities, which is a mixed-type investment product with a risk rating of Level 3.
Another surviving product is "Youyin Wealth Tianti · Hongjin Short Holding 365 Days No. 1", a fixed income type product. It started fundraising on December 30 last year and officially commenced operations on January 4 this year. Its cumulative net value was 1.0011 on February 8.
According to the Opinions of the State Council's Office on Promoting the Development of Personal Pension Plans, the funds in personal pension accounts can be invested in financial products such as bank wealth management products, savings deposits, commercial endowment insurance, and public offering funds.
The launch of the first batch of individual pension product funds marks the beginning of individual pension investors being able to officially purchase fund products through their individual pension account.
In November last year, the CBIRC issued the "Provisional Measures for the Management of Individual Pension Business by Commercial Banks and Wealth Management Companies."
The method stipulates that participants can purchase various personal pension products, such as personal pension savings, personal pension investment products, personal pension insurance products, and public offering fund products of personal pensions, through their personal pension account.
Subsequently, the Ministry of Human Resources and Social Security, the Ministry of Finance, and the State Taxation Administration issued a notice, clearly stating that the individual pension system will be implemented in 36 pilot cities and regions, including Beijing, Tianjin, Shijiazhuang and Xiong'an New Area in Hebei Province, Jincheng City in Shanxi Province, and others.
As of the end of 2022, the number of individuals participating in the individual pension scheme was 19.54 million, with 6.13 million people contributing, and the total amount of contributions reached 14.2 billion yuan.
Previously, banks participating in the pilot program only listed three types of products: individual pension savings, individual pension insurance products, and public offering funds for individual pensions.
Now that a variety of individual pension investment products are available, how should investors choose?
Experts from the Product Development Department of Jiaoyin Wealth Management Products have stated that, compared to other personal pension products, both the pilot-style old-age security financial products and the personal pension financial products in the pilot phase have three main characteristics.
First, it is about stability. The risk management mechanism is more sound, the investment strategy and concepts are more prudent, and a third-party independent custody by non-parent institutions is implemented.
Secondly, it has a long-term nature. The term of pension wealth management products in the pilot phase is all 5 years or more. The next phase's individual pension wealth management products will have a minimum holding period of 1 year in principle, with encouragement to hold for 3 years or more.
Thirdly, it has inclusiveness. The purchase threshold for products is low, with the starting amount usually set at 1 yuan, and some as low as 0.01 yuan. The custody fees, management fees, and other related rates for the products are more favorable.
Experts point out that investors should choose products based on their characteristics and their own risk tolerance.
Individual pension savings have the characteristics of long-term duration, higher interest rates, and high safety, making them suitable for people with low risk tolerance. Personal pension insurance products focus on protection and are more suitable for individuals who cannot bear investment risks but can accept stable returns. In contrast, personal pension investment products and publicly offered fund products do not guarantee principal or returns and carry some investment risks, but they offer higher expected returns and are suitable for people with a certain level of financial knowledge and higher risk tolerance.
