2004 Indian Ocean Earthquake
On December 26, 2004, an earthquake occurred 160 kilometers west of Aceh Province on the island of Sumatra, Indonesia. The earthquake had a depth of 30 kilometers and a moment magnitude of 9.1 to 9.3.
The earthquake triggered a massive tsunami with wave heights reaching 15 to 30 meters.
A total of 14 countries along the Pacific coast were affected, with the most severely hit areas including Aceh Province in Indonesia, the Phuket and Krabi tourist areas in Thailand, Sri Lanka, and the Tamil Nadu region in India.
