A: The U.S. Department of Labor released the January 2023 nonfarm payrolls data on February 3. The number of new nonfarm jobs added was 517,000, significantly higher than the market's expected 189,000. The unemployment rate fell to 3.4%, the lowest level in nearly 50 years. Hourly wages grew by 4.4% year-over-year and 0.3% month-over-month, showing a slight slowdown.
From a total perspective, this data is affected by many one-time and technical factors, such as the return of teachers and staff who were on strike, adjustments in the survey statistics口径, and updates to the seasonal adjustment factors. Subsequent revisions may occur (refer to the case of January 2022, where the newly added non-farm payrolls of 504,000 were revised down to 364,000). Therefore, non-farm payrolls may not be as strong as the data suggests.
From a structural perspective, the impact of layoffs in high-tech enterprises is still present, but the proportion is relatively low; in contrast, sectors with high contactivity such as leisure hotels and education and health services have seen a significant rebound in new job creation. The data shows that there is still a labor shortage in the service sector.
Combining with the rebound in the PMI of the services sector, the rise in job vacancies and the narrowing of the labor shortage, as well as the strong performance of consumer credit data, we judge that after the extreme weather and holidays, the U.S. services sector is experiencing a rapid recovery.
We believe that it is difficult for the tight labor market in the United States to improve without a downturn.
Currently, there is still a supply gap of more than 5 million in the U.S. labor market, and the labor participation rate is rising slowly. Especially for the labor participation rate of people aged 25-54, it has already approached the high level before the pandemic.
In addition, due to the strong savings and consumption credit of American residents, the strong demand for consumption will further delay the impact of tight policies on the job market.
The continued tightness of the labor market supply and demand will be the main color of the U.S. economy in 2023.
Considering the current situation approaching the end of rate hikes and the persistent fluctuations in inflation expectations, we are not optimistic about the continued decline in wage growth.
Before the release of this data, the U.S. stock, bond, and currency markets had been overly optimistic about the Federal Reserve's path of interest rate hikes.
With the continuous improvement of inflation data, the Federal Reserve has been tightening its hiking pace while maintaining a delicate balance of market inflation expectations. However, market participants have ignored the Fed's pro-eagle (hawkish) statements, expecting not only an early halt to rate hikes but also two rate cuts by the end of the year.
In the context of tight labor market supply and demand and the uncertain impact of tightening policies, we believe that the Federal Reserve's guidance on rate hikes at the end of the year is relatively reasonable. However, the adjustment of market extreme expectations and the congestion in trading may pose certain harm to the market.
Despite this, the stubbornly high wage growth has not been able to reverse the rapid decline in current inflation. With the M2 data turning negative year-on-year and the gradual improvement of leading CPI sub-indexes, since October the US CPI data has already entered a phase of rapid decline. The stubbornly high wage growth can only serve as a floor for future inflation data. The current market expectations are difficult to disprove. After the next round of inflation data is released, the market may enter a new round of speculation.
Founder of Shanshan Group Zheng Yonggang died suddenly from a cardiac disease. He once led China's top clothing stock to transform. - Economic Observation Network - Professional Financial and Economic News Website
Economic Observation Network reporter Zheng Yuxin. On February 11, a WeChat official account of Ssangyong Holding Co., Ltd. (hereinafter referred to as "Ssangyong Holding") issued a notice of mourning. It was announced that the founder of Ssangyong Group and the chairman of the Board of Directors of Ssangyong Holding, Zheng Yonggang, died on February 10, 2023, due to sudden cardiac disease, after receiving treatment without improvement. He was 65 years old at the time of his death.
In the 1980s, Zheng Yonggang served as the manager of a state-owned cotton spinning factory. When he was transferred, in 1989 he became the manager of the predecessor of Shanshan Co., Ltd., Ningbo Yungang Textile Factory.
In December 2022, at the 20th China Enterprise Leaders' Conference and the 22nd China Enterprise Star of the Future Conference, Zheng Yonggang said in his speech that in the Chinese men's suit market in the 1990s, the market share of Shanshan brand reached as high as 37%.
Shanshan Group (600884.SH) went public in 1996, making it the first clothing company in China to list on the stock market.
Just when the clothing business was thriving, Ssangyong Group began to transform. This was because Zheng Yonggang realized that "once the market opens up, Chinese brands will naturally form a tiered brand market. It is unlikely that Ssangyong suits will continue to lead the trend and remain a national clothing brand for the Chinese people for the long term."
In 1999, Shanshan began to study corporate transformation. Zheng Yonggang recalled at that time, "We came to Shanghai to figure out what kind of transformation we should pursue. We specifically sought out many experts and scholars and held a series of 'Zhuge Liang meetings' and abstract study seminars continuously."
Finally, we have set two major strategic directions.
The first direction is new energy and new materials, and the other is big health, which has a bright future.
After the strategic direction was determined, Suan Suan began to seek partnerships. At that time, the Carbonaceous Materials Research Institute of Anshan Thermal Energy Institute was working on a national 863 project to support Anshan Iron & Steel. However, the research funding was insufficient. Therefore, Suan Suan and the Carbonaceous Materials Research Institute of Anshan Thermal Energy Institute signed a cooperation agreement to jointly promote the industrialization of the national 863 project "Intermediate Phase Carbon Microspheres." They then engaged in the research, development, production, and sales of anode materials, achieving the commercial promotion of anode materials domestically.
In 2001, Suan Suan Shares achieved the large-scale production of mesophase carbon microspheres and began to replace imported products domestically, becoming the main supplier of mesophase carbon microspheres in China, taking the place of Japan.
This is the first lithium-ion battery anode material production enterprise in China, achieving the domestic production of lithium-ion battery anode materials.
With the rapid popularization of lithium batteries, Shanshan Co., Ltd.'s lithium battery business has begun to develop gradually. In 2007, the lithium battery materials business was written into the main business of Shanshan Co., Ltd. The revenue share of the clothing business has been decreasing year by year, until 2013, when the revenue from the lithium battery materials business of Shanshan Co., Ltd. completely surpassed that of the clothing business.
In February 2021, Shanshan Group successfully acquired LG Chem's polarizer business and entered the LCD polarizer market, establishing Shangjin Optoelectronics Co., Ltd. in the polarizer sector. This field has a high level of technical complexity. Shanshan's main competitors are global 500 companies, such as Samsung of South Korea, Sumitomo Chemical and Nikko Electric of Japan.
Zheng Yonggang once shared his insights on post-investment management, saying, "The success rate of Chinese private enterprises acquiring some high-tech companies abroad is relatively low. Why do these acquisitions often fail?"
"Because everyone will consider this, I have spent so much money, so I need to send people to manage it, right? This is a usual action," he said. However, Zheng Yonggang was different. On the day of the successful acquisition of Sasan, Zheng Yonggang announced to the public at Sasan Optoelectronics that Sasan would implement a "one enterprise, two systems" policy as the major shareholder of Sasan. Except for Zheng Yonggang serving as chairman, no personnel from Sasan Enterprise would be sent to Sasan. Instead, it would be operated through authorization. The original distribution system, corporate culture, and various management models would remain unchanged.
ICC Xinluo Information released the 2022 negative electrode data. According to the data, Suan Suan Negative Electrode achieved an outbound volume of over 2 million tons in 2022, a year-on-year increase of 100%, with a market share of 16%. The output of artificial graphitic negative electrode materials has remained number one.
According to Yano Research's statistics in the polarizer business, the company's Sajin Optoelectronics accounted for 29% of the global market share in 2022, and is expected to reach 32% in 2023, maintaining its position as the global leader.
In the first three quarters of 2022, Ssangyong Shares' revenue was 15.841 billion yuan, and its net profit was 2.313 billion yuan. On February 10th, the stock price of Ssangyong Shares was 19.24 yuan per share, with a total market capitalization of 43.6 billion yuan.
On February 9th, Shanshan Shares stated on its interactive platform that as of the end of 2022, the company's effective graphite production capacity was about 100,000 tons. The graphite production capacity of the Meishan project is still in the process of increasing.
Wande shows that Zheng Yonggang is still the chairman and actual controller of Ssangyong Shares.
The Tianyancha shows that Zheng Yonggang holds 40.1% of the total equity in Ssangyong Holding Co., Ltd.
Li Zhihua is the general manager of Shanshan Co., Ltd. He was born in 1968. He has previously served as the chairman of Shanshan Battery Materials Co., Ltd. in Dongguan City, Shanshan New Materials Technology Co., Ltd. in Ningshan, Shanshan Energy Technology Co., Ltd. in Hunan Province, and vice president of Shanshan Co., Ltd. in Ningshan.
On February 10, Shanshan Shares stated on its investor interaction platform that there are no close family relationships between the company's senior management and its actual controller.
"Fund E Account" Arrives: CSRC Authorizes Development to Enable Investors to Aggregate and Query All Funds under Their Name - Economic Observer - Professional Financial News Website
China Economic Weekly reporter Chen Shan: Is it difficult to aggregate account information due to the complex purchasing channels of funds?
Always forgetting the "small treasury"?
These issues facing the grassroots people will be resolved soon.
On February 10th, the CSRC announced that the "Fund E Account" APP has been launched on various mobile app stores and is now conducting a public trial operation.
According to the introduction, the "Fund E Account" provides a "one-stop" query service for individual investors regarding public fund accounts and share information, aiming to address industry service pain points such as investors forgetting their accounts and the inconvenience of querying information.
According to data from Wind, as of the end of 2022, there were 156 fund management companies in China that issued public funds, managing a total asset scale of about 26 trillion yuan; there were 167 fund registration institutions and 411 fund sales institutions for public funds.
Each share registration and settlement institution's account system is independent, and there is a lack of a unified industry query channel.
Some industry professionals stated that as of the end of 2021, the number of fund investors in our country exceeded 720 million, meaning that half of the population in the country has invested in fund products.
Previously, investors had to check their purchase records through different sales institutions. With the "Fund E Account," they can query the purchase details from all sales channels, making it clear at a glance how many funds they hold.
"Fund E Account" app is what?
According to relevant documents, the "Fund E Account" APP is a mobile application developed by China Securities Depository and Clearing Co., Ltd. with approval from the China Securities Regulatory Commission. It serves as a mobile portal for the public fund industry and provides investors with a one-stop query service for their holdings of off-exchange shares of all public fund products in the market.
Investors can conveniently and efficiently understand the holdings of their offline shares in various publicly offered fund products of different fund management companies through the "Fund E Account," regardless of which sales channels they purchased them through across the entire market, thereby significantly improving query efficiency.
Specifically, investors can query the following information through the "Fund E Account": information about their fund accounts opened with all public fund management companies across the market, information about their trading accounts opened with public fund sales institutions, as well as details about their holdings of off-exchange shares in products such as publicly offered securities投资基金 and collective asset management plans established and managed by securities companies, where the number of investors is not restricted to 200 people.
Li Yiqian, business director of the Shanghai Stock Exchange Fund Evaluation Research Center, told the Economic Observation Network that investors can use the "Fund E Account" app to learn about all their holdings of off-exchange public funds in one go. This helps them find "forgotten assets." More importantly, it aggregates all fund investment information across accounts for customers, helping them more timely, accurate, and comprehensively understand their own investment situations. This enables customers to better optimize their fund portfolio configurations and better plan their financial arrangements.
How to register and use it?
The reporter noticed that the "Fund E Account" app has been launched on app stores of major phone brands such as Huawei, Apple, Xiaomi, OPPO, and Vivo. However, the app is still in the public testing phase. Registration requires an invitation code, and investors can contact the fund management company of the fund they hold to obtain it.
A customer service representative from a medium-to-large-scale public fund company in Shanghai provided a six-digit invitation code to journalists from Economic Observation Network and told them, "During the trial operation phase of the APP, China Securities Depository and Clearing Co., Ltd. provides each fund manager with a certain number of invitation codes. Investors can call to obtain them, and we will provide them."
After the trial operation is completed, users will no longer need an invitation code when registering.
This project requires more financial support, so we need to apply for additional funding from the government.
According to the "Fund E Account" download and usage instructions published on the CSRC website, the journalist registered the account and completed the query process, which took only a few minutes. The entire process mainly consisted of four steps: user registration, real-name verification, fund account binding, and public fund inquiry.
After completing the real-name verification step, click the "Assets" fund binding button. All the fund products purchased by the journalist through various fund sales platforms will be displayed in the binding options list (available for binding). After completing the binding, you can clearly see the total assets of the invested funds and start using the query functions.
It is worth noting that the "Fund E Account" only provides query services for investors and cannot be used for subscription, redemption, or trading.
"Fund E Account" displays data that is generally three trading days before the date on which the user queries (T day).
For example, on February 10th, when you open the "Fund E Account," the total assets, number of fund shares, and net asset value displayed on the asset page correspond to the date three trading days before February 10th, i.e., February 7th.
