VNA Hanoi – VNA Correspondent Report: During his visit to Brunei Darussalam, Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh and his wife visited the University of Brunei Darussalam (UBD, also known as "Brunei University") in the morning of February 11.
British University is the largest higher education and scientific research center in Brunei and ranks third among universities in the region.
British University is one of the symbols of educational and training cooperation between Vietnam and Brunei.
British University established formal cooperation with FPT University in Vietnam in July 2013, with the main area of cooperation being English training.
In addition to English, French, ethics, Japanese, and Korean, the University of Brunei also includes Vietnamese in its teaching curriculum.
When visiting the University of Brunei, Prime Minister of Vietnam Pham Minh Chinh and his wife had a conversation with students in the Vietnamese language class.
Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh is happy that an increasing number of foreigners are interested in learning Vietnamese. He has made positive contributions to promoting the unique cultural characteristics and local customs of Vietnam around the world.
Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh expressed confidence and hope that the Vietnamese teaching staff at Brunei University will continue to grow stronger. He noted that students in the Vietnamese language class are increasingly interested in learning Vietnamese, striving to study hard and soon be able to speak Vietnamese fluently, becoming messengers of the friendly cooperation between Vietnam and Brunei.
Taking this opportunity, Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh also held a video call with Vietnamese students studying English at the FPT-UBD Global Center in Da Nang, to understand their learning situation, especially during the pandemic.
Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh believes that the cooperation between the Vietnam FPT University and Brunei University, especially the FPT-UBD Global Center, is a vivid symbol of the educational cooperation between Vietnam and Brunei.
At the same time, it is hoped that the students of the center will make greater progress in their studies and make positive contributions to the friendly cooperation between Vietnam and the other country.
Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh highly praised the achievements of bilateral education cooperation during his discussion with the Minister of Education of Brunei and leaders of Brunei University. This included the cooperation between FPT University and Brunei University, as well as Brunei University's decision to include Vietnamese in its teaching curriculum.
Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh hopes that the University of Brunei will continue to focus on ensuring the quality of Vietnamese language teaching and further expand the scale of the Vietnamese language classes.
Vice Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh highly praised the positive results of the cooperation between the two countries based on the Memorandum of Understanding on Educational Cooperation signed in April 2014. He suggested that Brunei continue to provide more scholarships and effectively implement various short-term exchange training programs, such as the Global Discovery Programme and the Discovery Year.
Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh highly praised the establishment of the first branch of the University of Brunei in Southeast Asia by the University of Brunei; he believes that the university is growing stronger in scale and influence both regionally and globally; and he looks forward to further expanding cooperation with Vietnamese higher education institutions.
The Prime Minister and his wife, Pham Minh Chinh, planted a memorial tree in the campus of Brunei University and wrote messages in the memorial book.
Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh wishes the University of Brunei continued growth and development, and to contribute even more significantly to Brunei's educational cause. He also hopes to deepen and broaden cooperation with educational training institutions in Vietnam.
(End)
