VOV News - Hanoi - VOV News Correspondent reports: The official visit of Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh and his wife to Singapore and Brunei has been successfully completed and has achieved comprehensive, practical and specific results.
The Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh participated in more than 30 different activities within three days of his visit to Singapore and Brunei.
The achievements have injected new momentum into the continuous development of the strategic partnership between Vietnam and the United States and the comprehensive partnership between Vietnam and Vietnam.
During his visit to the two countries, Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh continued to reaffirm the foreign policy of the Vietnamese Party and State, namely independence, diversity, and adaptability, and expressed the willingness to be a good friend and reliable partner to all countries and a responsible member of the international community.
Strengthening relations with Singapore and Brunei is in the interest of both countries, aimed at promoting the well-being of the people of both nations and contributing to peace, stability, and development in the region and around the world.
At the various meetings and talks, Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh reached a consensus with the leaders of Singapore and Brunei to enhance political mutual trust between the two countries through measures such as mutual visits of high-level delegations, effectively implementing various bilateral cooperation mechanisms and important bilateral cooperation agreements.
Many cooperation documents were signed during this visit.
Among them, the Memorandum of Understanding on the Green and Digital Economy Partnership with Singapore and the Action Plan for Strengthening the Comprehensive Partnership between Vietnam and Brunei for the 2023-2027 Period are the two major highlights.
The Vietnam-Singapore Green and Digital Economy Partnership Memorandum of Understanding is signed.
Image from VNA
During meetings with business leaders, at seminars or when attending economic forums, Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh emphasized that Vietnam welcomes and creates convenient conditions for investments by Singaporean and Bruneian enterprises in areas such as digital transformation, green energy, high-tech, and innovation and creativity.
This visit not only helps deepen cooperation between Vietnam, Singapore, and Brunei in various traditional areas such as politics, diplomacy, economy, security, defense, education and training, oil and gas, tourism, and people-to-people exchanges, but also establishes a framework for cooperation in new potential areas such as the digital economy, green economy, energy transition, innovation and creativity, smart cities, and sustainable development.
The Sultan of Brunei, Hassanal Bolkiah, and Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh are preparing to enter the bilateral dialogue session.
Image courtesy of VNA
During his visit to the two countries, Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh arranged time to visit and listen to the thoughts and wishes of the Vietnamese communities living abroad.
At the meetings between the leaders of the two countries, Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh has always suggested that the authorities of both countries pay more attention to ensuring that the local Vietnamese communities are treated fairly, and create favorable conditions for them to contribute to local society and to foster bilateral relations.
The proposal has been agreed to and supported by leaders of both countries.
Particularly, Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh also shared with the leaders of both countries their desire for an ASEAN community that is united, peaceful, stable, and prosperous; he also reached a consensus with the leaders of ASEAN countries to maintain unity and cooperation, and to enhance ASEAN's central role in the complex and ever-changing regional and international situation.
Thanks to the significant achievements obtained, Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh's official visit to Singapore and Brunei has made positive contributions to effectively implementing the foreign policy priorities of the 13th Party Congress, which emphasizes strengthening relations with ASEAN neighbors; effectively implementing Resolution 12-KL/TW of the Central Committee of the Party on the work of overseas Vietnamese affairs in the new situation; and mobilizing the strength of the entire nation to unite.
